{"ticker":"BAJAJHIND","symbol":"BAJAJHIND","instrumentId":3022336,"name":"Bajaj Hindusthan","industry":"NSE-Food-Packaged","about":"Bajaj Hindusthan Sugar Ltd. is a leading sugar and ethanol manufacturing company in India, with 14 state-of-the-art sugar mills located in Uttar Pradesh. The company produces a wide range of products, including refined and raw sugar, ethanol, and renewable power, primarily generated from bagasse, a sugarcane by-product. Bajaj Hindusthan caters to industrial, commercial, and retail markets, supplying sugar to FMCG companies, distilleries, and export markets. The company emphasizes sustainable practices, focusing on energy efficiency and waste management to minimize its environmental impact. Bajaj Hindusthan’s integrated approach and large production capacity make it a key player in India’s sugar industry.","website":"www.bajajhindusthan.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:06:55.219Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":17.63,"changePct":3.8892162639952867,"week52High":24.23,"week52Low":14.93},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹4,215 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹5,144 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"2,079,879,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"68"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"1,235,947,276"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.00%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"5.04"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"380.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.03"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.95"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"0%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"9.23"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"12–313"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"15.3%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"0.97"},{"label":"Volume","value":"9,718,007"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"14,203,730"},{"label":"Master score","value":"34"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"31"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"37"},{"label":"Group rank","val